    "stdout_tail": "85-970a-65377bd09c24\",\n                      \"chunk_id\": \"a3a509a6e75df1887e535518c80e2e1bb412f051169bf7cfab75ae0ecfc63e7f\",\n                      \"chunk_fingerprint\": \"a3a509a6e75df1887e535518c80e2e1bb412f051169bf7cfab75ae0ecfc63e7f\",\n                      \"section\": \"YOLO9000: Better, Faster, Stronger / 5. Conclusion\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                      \"quote_text\": \"geNet detection task. The detection task for ImageNet shares on 44 object categories with COCO which means that YOLO9000 has only seen classification data for the majority of the test images, not detection data. YOLO9000 gets 19.7 mAP overall with 16.0 mAP on the disjoint 156 object classes that it has never seen any labelled detection data for. This mAP is higher than results achieved by DPM but YOLO9000 is trained on different datasets with only partial supervision [4]. It also is simultaneously detecting 9000 other object categories, all in real-time.\\n\\nWhen we analyze YOLO9000’s performance on ImageNet we see it learns new species of animals well but struggles with learning categories like clothing and equipment.\\n\\n<!-- Image (Table 7) -->\\nTable 7: YOLO9000 Best and Worst Classes on Imag\",\n                      \"work_id\": \"cda6a480-8512-4b85-970a-65377bd09c24\",\n                      \"chunk_id\": \"365643e902b4bacf366798a08b0c04d2db02c564958015ee96915fb547543cb5\",\n                      \"chunk_fingerprint\": \"365643e902b4bacf366798a08b0c04d2db02c564958015ee96915fb547543cb5\",\n                      \"section\": \"YOLO9000: Better, Faster, Stronger\"\n                    },\n                    {\n                      \"quote_text\": \"## 1. Introduction\\n\\nGeneral purpose object detection should be fast, accurate, and able to recognize a wide variety of objects. Since the introduction of neural networks, detection frameworks have become increasingly fast and accurate. However, most detection methods are still constrained to a small set of objects.\\n\\nCurrent object detection datasets are limited compared to datasets for other tasks like classification and tagging. The most common detection datasets contain thousands to hundreds of thousands of images with dozens to hundreds of tags [3] [10] [2]. Classification datasets have millions of images with tens or hundreds of thousands of categories [20] [2].\\n\\nWe would like detection to scale to level of object classification. However, labelling images for detection is far more expe\",\n                      \"work_id\": \"cda6a480-8512-4b85-970a-65377bd09c24\",\n                      \"chunk_id\": \"a10513f3719a7e6dc3b8a26ed05dc2920628f6304eb92f40c047e1f9bc820bc0\",\n                      \"chunk_fingerprint\": \"a10513f3719a7e6dc3b8a26ed05dc2920628f6304eb92f40c047e1f9bc820bc0\",\n                      \"section\": \"YOLO9000: Better, Faster, Stronger / 1. Introduction\"\n                    }\n                  ],\n                  \"row_count\": 5,\n                  \"truncated\": false\n                }\n              ],\n              \"evidence_origin\": \"parent_tool\",\n              \"confidence\": 0.9,\n              \"terminal_state\": \"succeeded\",\n              \"failure_code\": null\n            }\n          ],\n          \"merge\": {\n            \"evidence_origin\": \"parent_tool\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.9,\n            \"conflict\": null,\n            \"writer_directive\": \"Evidence merge (v3): synthesize a single grounded answer. evidence_origin='parent_tool'. Do not hide tool denials, timeouts, or conflicting VERDICT lines; state them explicitly.\",\n            \"partial_failure\": false\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"run_kind\": \"supervisor_specialists_v3\",\n      \"graph_id\": \"supervisor_graph_v3\",\n      \"tool_search_shortlist_ratio_avg\": 0.7143,\n      \"tool_search_deferred_schema_events\": null,\n      \"budget_stop_reasons\": [],\n      \"answer_class\": \"g